# ChangeKey on the application master key really replaces the key: after the
# change the old key no longer authenticates, the new one does, GetKeyVersion
# reports the new version, and changing back restores the original.
#
# Generated from tests/test_dfc_virtual_picc_mutation_vectors.c
# (/pcsc-change-key-mutation-proves-auth-behavior) by recording the exchanges the
# reference engine performed, then cross-checked: all 16 byte
# expectations asserted by that test matched the recording exactly.
# 6 further exchanges carry no byte expectation in the source.
#
# The ChangeKey cryptograms are computed at runtime by the original test
# from the derived session key, so they are recorded rather than
# transcribed. inject-random pins RndB ahead of every authentication so
# the vector does not depend on the engine's default generator.

